hOjAPnHgWQE,Sattva | Raga Hamsadhwani | Exploration and improvisation on Sitar,"Raga Hamsadhwani is a beautiful Raga which draws inspiration from Carnatic Music. A raga under the thaat Bilawal, it is similar to the western Ionian mode (a subset of Ionian, in fact). Hamsadhwani literally translates to Sound of the swans. The presiding deity of the Raga is Lord Vishnu, source of Sattva, or positive, sublime energy. Hence, its name Sattva is an apt representation of its peaceful and sublime nature. The raga is traditionally performed in the evenings, and that's when the Raga has its maximum effect. The Raga's Rasa (emotional theme and mental state of the Raga) is auspicious.",UCLI9__KHyyVQqbeOVLyJGHw,Keshav Bimbraw,20161019,sitar; Hamsadhwani; Hindustani; Music; Classical Music,Music,305,640x480,2d,,public,not_live,True,Creative Commons Attribution license (reuse allowed),3070,72.0,6.0,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hOjAPnHgWQE,sitar/hOjAPnHgWQE.wav,sitar,False,real
